From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ilya Vysotsky <il.mohoff2016@yandex.ru>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:58:53 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 24/30] Video on feature level 9_3: DXVA frames stay on the GPU

Frames decoded by DXVA were read back to memory, converted and uploaded
again (three trips through the CPU per frame). Nothing on this device can
be shared, but nothing needs to be: the port is one process. Now, when
texture sharing does not work:
- the decoder works on the compositor's own device;
- frames are converted to BGRA by the video processor into plain textures
  (no NT handle, keyed mutex or fence) that reach the compositor by id
  through GpuProcessD3D11TextureMap, created in this process;
- software WebRender with the D3D11 compositor takes DXGI images, which
  become native compositor surfaces drawn by HandleExternalImage.
If the video processor or any of this fails on the phone, the decoder
falls back to reading frames back to memory, and the log says so.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
